    description: "## What\nA BlockNote (`@blocknote/core` + `@blocknote/react`, MPL-2.0, Yjs-native via y-prosemirror) editor bound to an item's discussion/notes Y.Text in the live Y.Doc, mounted as a React island inside the existing Lit scaffold in packages/htrac-frontend (or a React page, if the scaffold moves to React -- Excalidraw/BlockNote/xyflow are all React). Reads arrive via the Yjs sync endpoint (item D); writes persist only through the op bridge (item C), so an edit becomes a `discuss` op with attribution.\n## Why BlockNote\nClosest maintained equivalent of BlockSuite's block/page mode (0.56.0, 2026-10-14) now that the BlockSuite npm line is dormant (last publish 2025-07-01). It peers on both `yjs ^13.6` and `@y/y ^14-rc`; follow the ADR's version choice.\n## Done when\nTwo clients co-edit a discussion draft and the committed text appears in the ops log as a `discuss` op by the right author; the view degrades to read-only when the bridge is unavailable. Frontend typechecks and builds (no CI runs the frontend today -- state that in the PR and run it locally).\n## Context\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4."  # a77b
    fields: {}  # a77b
